This code will add an Open Graph meta tag for the featured image of your blog post. If you don't have a featured image set, you can use the `get_the_post_thumbnail_url()` function to get the first image in the post and use that as the Open Graph image.

Alternatively, you can use a plugin like "Yoast SEO" which has an option to add Open Graph meta tags to your blog posts. Simply install and activate the plugin, then go to the "Social" tab in the Yoast SEO settings and enable the "Open Graph" feature. From there, you can select the image you want to use as the Open Graph image for your blog post.

Once you've added the Open Graph meta tag, you should see the image displayed when you share your blog post on Facebook.

