To create a NestJS model that creates a MongoDB document with multiple schemas, you can use the `@nestjs/mongoose` package along with the `mongoose` library. Here's an example of how you can create a model with multiple schemas:

```typescript
// user.schema.ts
import { Schema } from 'mongoose';

export const userSchema = new Schema({
  name: String,
  email: String,
});

// post.schema.ts
import { Schema } from 'mongoose';

export const postSchema = new Schema({
  title: String,
  content: String,
  author: { type: Schema.Types.ObjectId, ref: 'User' },
});

// blog.schema.ts
import { Schema } from 'mongoose';
import { User } from './user.schema';
import { Post } from './post.schema';

export const blogSchema = new Schema({
  title: String,
  content: String,
  author: { type: Schema.Types.ObjectId, ref: 'User' },
  posts: [Post],
});

// blog.model.ts
import { Model, model, Schema } from 'mongoose';
import { Blog } from './blog.schema';

export const BlogModel: Model<Blog> = model('Blog', blogSchema);
```

