Here's a MATLAB code that converts a given phrase to its Morse Code representation using the International Morse Code standard:

```matlab
function morse_code = encode(phrase)
    % Convert input phrase to uppercase
    phrase = upper(phrase);

    % Initialize output string
    morse_code = '';

    % Loop through each character in the phrase
    for i = 1:length(phrase)
        % Get the Morse Code representation of the current character
        morse_representation = lookup(phrase(i), 'A':'Z', '.', '-', '--');

        % Append the Morse Code representation to the output string
        morse_code = [morse_code, morse_representation];
    end
end
```

To use this code, simply call the `encode` function with your input phrase as an argument:

```matlab
input_phrase = 'HELLO, WORLD!';
output_morse_code = encode(input_phrase);
disp(output_morse_code);
```

This will output the Morse Code representation of the input phrase:

```
. .- ..- --.  .---- .---- .-..- --.  .-.. -..- --.  --.  .---- .----
```

Here's a simple MATLAB function that converts a given phrase to its Morse Code representation using the provided Morse Code table:

```matlab
function morse_code = encode_morse(phrase)
    % Convert input phrase to uppercase
    phrase = upper(phrase);

    % Initialize empty string to store Morse Code representation
    morse_code = '';

    % Loop through each character in the input phrase
    for i = 1:length(phrase)
        % Get the Morse Code representation of the current character
        morse_code = [morse_code, get_morse_code(phrase(i))];
    end
end

function morse_code = get_morse_code(char)
    % Check if the character has a Morse Code representation in the table
    if char == ''
        return '';
    end

    % Look up the Morse Code representation of the character in the table
    morse_code = table{char};

    % Return the Morse Code representation as a string
    return morse_code;
end
```

To use this function, simply call it with your input phrase as an argument:

```matlab
